# Portfolio Design System: Editorial Cream Style

Oct 5, 2026 · @MAYOR

---

## 1. Purpose and principles

This doc specifies a single-page developer portfolio style: warm cream paper background, a high-contrast serif for headlines with one coral italic word per heading, small monospace labels, hairline rules, pastel app cards, and one dark navy section for contrast. It is reverse-engineered from the reference portfolio kiddobuild.dev (screenshots, October 2026). All values are estimates read from screenshots; confirm exact numbers in DevTools before shipping. Use this doc as the single source when designing new pages, sections or components in this style.

### Five rules that define the look

1. **Cream, not white.** Page background is `#f1efe7`; pure white appears only inside cards and device mockups.
2. **Serif headline, one italic accent word or phrase in coral per heading.** Never italicize a whole heading.
3. **Structure is drawn with 1px hairlines and mono micro-labels,** not with boxes, shadows or gradients.
4. **Color is rationed:** neutrals everywhere, coral for emphasis, pastels only on app tiles, navy for one full-width section.
5. **Large radius on media and panels, pill shape on buttons and nav,** square-ish on nothing.

**Content model.** Every section carries: a mono section label (number + name), a serif title with italic accent, a one-line supporting sentence in muted grey, then the content block.

