## 4. Global chrome

Three persistent elements frame the page: a quiet top header, a floating bottom pill nav, and a contextual "skip" chip. Placement is estimated from the screenshots.

| Element | Placement | Spec |
|---|---|---|
| Header bar | Top of page, not sticky, 24px top padding | Three zones. Left: name in serif 20px over a mono sub-label (role). Center: two short mono lines (location or availability, last-updated date). Right: mono line (local time or status). Bottom edge: 1px `--line` rule |
| Anchor row | Directly under header, above hero | Mono 11px uppercase links separated by 24px gaps (Home, Apps, Work, Capabilities, Contact). `--muted`, hover `--ink` |
| Floating nav | Fixed, bottom center, 24px from viewport bottom | Pill, `--r-pill`, background `--ink` or `--paper` with 1px `--line`, height 48px, padding 6px, `--shadow-float`. Contains 2–4 items: icon-only links plus one filled primary pill ("Book a call") |
| Skip chip | Fixed, bottom left, appears from section 3 onward | Small pill, mono 10px uppercase label ("Skip to live apps"), 1px `--line`, background `--paper`. Jumps to the apps section |
| Section counters | Inside each section header row | Mono, `NN — NAME`, number in `--accent` |

### Rules

- Only the floating nav and skip chip are fixed. Nothing else sticks.
- Floating nav hides on scroll down inside the footer and reappears on scroll up.
- On `--navy` sections the floating nav keeps its own background so it stays legible; do not recolor it per section.
- Header contents are text only: no logo mark, no hamburger on desktop.

