## 5. Section specs

Placement and content slots for each section, top to bottom.

### 5.1 Hero

- Slot order: H1, supporting paragraph, CTA row, three-line principles list, illustration panel, italic caption.
- **H1:** two lines, left aligned, columns 1–8. Accent phrase on the second line ("actually use.").
- **Supporting paragraph:** 16px `--muted`, max width 520px, 24px under H1.
- **CTA row:** primary pill (fill `--ink`, text `--paper`, height 44px, padding 0 20px) plus a text link with an arrow, 12px gap, 32px under the paragraph.
- **Principles list:** three rows, each a 1px `--line` top border, mono 11px label left and a short sentence right, 12px vertical padding.
- **Illustration panel:** full container width, radius `--r-panel`, dark background in the `--navy` family, height about 420px desktop. Flat vector scene: a central character, an orbit ellipse, two floating cubes, small mono HUD labels in the corners (coordinates, status). Accent orange used on two or three shapes only.
- **Caption:** serif italic 15px, `--muted`, right aligned, 16px under the panel.

### 5.2 Apps

- Header pattern from section 3, title "Seen on real home screens." with accent on "home screens."
- Content is a card grid or a list. Both variants are specified in section 7.

### 5.3 Product showcases

- Header pattern, title "Products with a point of view."
- One block per product, 128px between blocks. Each block has the same text stack, then media:
  - a. Mono meta row: `NN — CATEGORY` left, `YEAR · PLATFORM` right.
  - b. Serif H3 (product name).
  - c. One-line tagline, `--muted`, max 640px.
  - d. Mono tag row (stack or keywords), pill outlines, 8px gap.
  - e. Text link "See product →".
  - f. Media.
- Media patterns, alternated down the page:
  - **Wide panel:** one full-width panel, radius `--r-panel`, saturated flat background (orange, navy) with a mockup or photo card overlapping the panel edge.
  - **Pair:** two panels side by side, 50/50 minus 24px gap, each with a portrait phone screenshot centered, title and one-line description under each.
  - **Single:** one panel at 60–70% width, left aligned, with a screenshot or video still.

### 5.4 Capabilities (dark)

- Background `--navy`, 128px vertical padding, text `--paper`.
- Header pattern with `--navy-line` rule. Title "One product brain. Four ways to ship." with accent on the second sentence.
- 2×2 grid, outer radius `--r-card`, tiles divided by shared 1px `--navy-line` hairlines (no gaps, no inner radius).
- Tile: line icon 24px top left, serif title 28px, 2–3 lines of `--navy-muted` body, mono tag row at the bottom. Tile padding 32px, min height 280px.
- Titles used: Mobile products, AI agents, Web products, Desktop and systems.

### 5.5 Closing CTA

- Centered stack on `--paper`: mono label, serif H2 ("The best work starts with a useful conversation.", accent on "useful conversation."), one supporting sentence (max 480px), one primary pill ("Book 20 minutes"), mono microcopy under it.

### 5.6 Footer

- Single row, 1px top `--line`, 24px padding. Mono 11px links left (email, social handles), copyright right. No columns, no newsletter field.

