## 6. Components

| Component | Anatomy and size | Default | Hover / focus |
|---|---|---|---|
| Primary button | Pill, height 44px, padding 0 20px, Inter 14px 500, optional 16px trailing arrow | Fill `--ink`, text `--paper` | Fill lifts to `#2a2a2a`, arrow moves 3px right. Focus ring: 2px `--accent`, 2px offset |
| Text link | Inter 14px 500, trailing arrow, 1px underline offset 4px | `--ink`, underline `--line` | Underline turns `--ink`, arrow moves 3px right |
| Pill tag | Height 26px, padding 0 10px, mono 10px uppercase, 1px `--line` border, transparent fill | `--muted` | `--ink` text, border `--ink` |
| Mono label | Mono 11px uppercase, 0.12em tracking, optional number in `--accent` | `--muted` | None |
| Round icon button | 36px circle, 1px `--line` border, 16px icon | `--ink` icon | Fill `--ink`, icon `--paper` |
| App icon | Square, 56px (list) or 64px (card), radius 22% | Flat color tile with simple glyph | Scale 1.04 |
| App card (variant 1) | Radius `--r-card`, padding 24px, min height 240px. Top: icon. Middle: serif 24px name, one-line Inter 14px description. Bottom: store buttons as small pills | Fill = one `--tile-*` tint, no border | Lifts 4px (translateY), no shadow change |
| App row (variant 2) | Full width, height 88px, 1px `--line` top and bottom. Columns: icon 56px, name + one-liner, platform tag, two round icon buttons | Transparent | Row background `rgba(20,20,20,.03)`, name gets accent underline |
| Showcase text stack | Section 5.3 order, left aligned, max width 640px | n/a | "See product →" follows text link rules |
| Capability tile | Section 5.4 | Transparent on navy | Background `rgba(255,255,255,.04)` |
| Floating nav | Section 4 | Pill, `--shadow-float` | Icon items: opacity .6 to 1 |

### Usage rules

- One primary button per viewport. Everything else is a text link or icon button.
- Never fill a pill tag. Never use more than 4 tags on one block.
- Icons are line icons, 1.5px stroke, 16 or 24px. No emoji, no filled icon sets.
- Focus states are always visible (accent ring). Hover alone never carries meaning.

