## 7. Apps section variants

The reference ships the apps section in more than one layout. The rest of the page (tokens, header, showcases, dark section, CTA) is identical across variants. Build the section as one component with a `variant` prop.

| | Style 1: pastel card grid | Style 2: hairline list |
|---|---|---|
| Section title | "Already on real home screens." (accent on "real home screens.") | "Seen on real home screens." (accent on "home screens.") |
| Following section title | "The right product, on the right surface." | "Products with a point of view." |
| Structure | One full-width featured card, then a 2-column grid | Single column list, 1 row per app |
| Item content | App icon, name, one-line description, store buttons | App icon, name, one-line description, platform tag, two round icon buttons |
| Item height | 220–260px | 88px |
| Background | One `--tile-*` tint per card, adjacent cards differ | `--paper`, hairline dividers |
| Grid gap | 16px | None (dividers only) |
| Height for 8 apps | About 1,100px desktop | About 700px desktop |
| Hover | Card lifts 4px | Row tint, name underline |
| Mobile | Single column, full-width cards | Same list, icon buttons collapse to one |
| Best for | 5–7 apps with distinct, colorful icons; visual first impression | 8+ apps; fast scanning; quieter page |

**Style 1 placement detail.** Featured card first (the strongest app), then pairs left to right. If the count is odd, the last card spans the full width. Card order = strength of the app, not alphabet.

**Style 2 placement detail.** Row columns on desktop: icon (56px) · name and description (flex 1) · platform tag (140px, right aligned) · icon buttons (96px). Description is one line, truncated with an ellipsis.

**Open item.** A third variant was mentioned but only two distinct layouts were provided as screenshots. Add it here as a third column when its screenshot is available.

