## 9. Responsive behavior

Mobile-first build, three breakpoints. Values are recommended; the reference screenshots confirm only that desktop and mobile layouts both stack to a single column with the same order.

| Breakpoint | Range | Layout changes |
|---|---|---|
| sm | <640px | 4-col grid, 20px side padding. Everything single column. Header collapses to name left, one mono line right. Anchor row hidden; floating nav carries navigation |
| md | 640–1023px | 8-col grid, 24px side padding. Showcase pairs stay side by side, apps cards 2 columns. Capability grid 2×2 |
| lg | ≥1024px | 12-col grid, 32px side padding, max width 1280px. All desktop specs apply |

### Element behavior

| Element | Mobile treatment |
|---|---|
| H1 / H2 / H3 | Sizes from the type table in section 2; use `clamp()` between breakpoints |
| Hero panel | Full width, height 260px, HUD labels reduced to two |
| CTA row | Primary pill full width, text link below |
| Section header row | Mono label and meta stack, rule stays |
| Showcase pair | Stacks, panels full width, 24px gap |
| Capability grid | Single column, tiles keep hairline dividers |
| Floating nav | Same pill, items limited to 3 |
| Skip chip | Hidden |
| Tap targets | Minimum 44×44px on all interactive elements |

